From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix, tracebacks freed by a subinterpreter corrupted the main interpreter heap

The traceback type is shared by every interpreter in the process, and its
deallocator is replaced at startup with one that keeps freed tracebacks on a
free list of its own, which has no lock. With subinterpreters running, e.g.
an InterpreterPoolExecutor, tracebacks that they free were put on it too:
objects from another interpreter's allocator, taken under another lock,
later reused and freed by the main interpreter. The process aborted with
"free(): invalid size" or segfaulted. A traceback that another interpreter
frees now goes to CPython's own deallocator.

Signed-off-by: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
---
 nuitka/build/static_src/InspectPatcher.c | changed
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nuitka/build/static_src/InspectPatcher.c b/nuitka/build/static_src/InspectPatcher.c
--- a/nuitka/build/static_src/InspectPatcher.c
+++ b/nuitka/build/static_src/InspectPatcher.c
@@ -644,8 +644,19 @@
 
     return result;
 }
+
+static destructor original_PyTraceBack_tp_dealloc = NULL;
 
 static void Nuitka_tb_dealloc(PyTracebackObject *tb) {
+    // The traceback type is shared by every interpreter in the process, but
+    // the free list below is the main interpreter's, and has no lock. A
+    // traceback another interpreter frees was allocated by that interpreter,
+    // under its own lock, so it must be freed the way CPython frees it.
+    if (unlikely(_PyInterpreterState_GET() != PyInterpreterState_Main())) {
+        original_PyTraceBack_tp_dealloc((PyObject *)tb);
+        return;
+    }
+
     // Need to use official method as it checks for recursion.
     Nuitka_GC_UnTrack(tb);
 
@@ -671,7 +682,12 @@
 #endif
 }
 
-void patchTracebackDealloc(void) { PyTraceBack_Type.tp_dealloc = (destructor)Nuitka_tb_dealloc; }
+void patchTracebackDealloc(void) {
+    if (original_PyTraceBack_tp_dealloc == NULL) {
+        original_PyTraceBack_tp_dealloc = PyTraceBack_Type.tp_dealloc;
+        PyTraceBack_Type.tp_dealloc = (destructor)Nuitka_tb_dealloc;
+    }
+}
 
 //     Part of "Nuitka", an optimizing Python compiler that is compatible and
 //     integrates with CPython, but also works on its own.
-- 
2.51.0

